  "corruptSays": [
    {
      "day": 2,
      "line": "The stash count is off. 1 stone missing. Nobody saw anything. Everybody suspects something."
    },
    {
      "day": 5,
      "line": "The stash count is off. 1 stone missing. Nobody saw anything. Everybody suspects something."
    },
    {
      "day": 6,
      "line": "The stash count is off. 1 stone missing. Nobody saw anything. Everybody suspects something."
    },
    {
      "day": 8,
      "line": "Devon looks at the pantry, then at the Codex, then at you. \"We’re going to make it.\" Haven will survive — because someone learned the land, and wrote it down. One less thing to fear."
    },
    {
      "day": 10,
      "line": "◈ FLASHBACK — Brass Locket\nBrass. Two photos inside, both fading. It opens with a click you can feel in your teeth — Esther's click, then your mother's, now yours."
    },
    {
      "day": 10,
      "line": "◈ FLASHBACK — Dispatcher's headset\nYou learned the voice — low, steady, unhurried. 'Panic is just information arriving too fast.' You hear it in your own voice now when it counts."
    },
    {
      "day": 10,
      "line": "◈ FLASHBACK — Trail compass\nLost above the fog line, visibility down to your boots. You didn't panic — just held the compass flat, found north, and walked out like it was nothing. It was not nothing."
    },
    {
      "day": 10,
      "line": "◈ FLASHBACK — Home key\nThe key never leaves your pocket. Locks are a promise: somewhere, a door still fits this."
    },
    {
      "day": 12,
      "line": "Word reaches you, days late: Ivana stands accused over what happened to Aroha. There's going to be a moot. People are choosing sides."
    },
    {
      "day": 13,
      "line": "Aroha has been talking at the fires. Enough voices — tonight they call a moot. Ivana answers for what happened to Aroha."
    },
    {
      "day": 13,
      "line": "Aroha calls the moot. The fire gets built up — word travels fast, and almost everyone comes."
    },
    {
      "day": 13,
      "line": "The moot turns to you. Your vote matters here — and everyone will remember it."
    },
    {
      "day": 15,
      "line": "The moot doesn't wait forever. Two days of silence from the fire's edge — the count is taken without you."
    },
    {
      "day": 20,
      "line": "Zoey leans in, voice low. \"Here's what we figured out about Hushpuppy. Wound the lead. Wound the lead and the pack breaks. Hit the FIRST wolf — the one that came in first — and the coordination dies. They fear fire, but breaking the lead is free.\""
    },
    {
      "day": 20,
      "line": "💡 COUNTER LEARNED — Hushpuppy: Wound the lead. Wound the lead and the pack breaks. Hit the FIRST wolf — the one that came in first — and the coordination dies. They fear fire, but breaking the lead is free. (Someone at the haven knew the trick.)"
    },
    {
      "day": 20,
      "line": "📓 Codex: Counter: Wound the lead — Wound the lead and the pack breaks. Hit the FIRST wolf — the one that came in first — and the coordination dies. They fear fire, but breaking the lead is free."
    },
    {
      "day": 25,
      "line": "💛 The Dispatcher's headset has become something you can reach for. (Keepsake L2 — new combat action: Steady. Hold it and breathe: clear fear and stun on yourself. Once per fight.)"
    },
    {
      "day": 27,
      "line": "💔 A faction of Stonebridge has turned cannibal — and split. The eaters walked. The Red Table is a new fire in the world now — 2 people under Theo."
    },
    {
      "day": 27,
      "line": "📓 Codex: Stonebridge split (cannibal). The Red Table formed; 3 petition at Haven's fire."
    },
    {
      "day": 27,
      "line": "They're named, every one: Kira Costa, Fatima Okafor, Maya Haddad. Your move — ask them questions (up to three), call a MOOT on it, or turn them away at the edge of the firelight."
    },
    {
      "day": 27,
      "line": "📓 Codex: 3 petitioners from Stonebridge (cannibal): Kira Costa, Fatima Okafor, Maya Haddad."
    },
    {
      "day": 30,
      "line": "They waited three days at the edge of your fire. Nobody called the moot. Kira nods — not angry, just done — and they walk."
    },
    {
      "day": 31,
      "line": "Devon showed Priya the huge smooth white ball sitting on the ground, sometimes head-sized — \"remember it.\" The haven hears about it by supper."
    },
    {
      "day": 31,
      "line": "Priya showed Aubrey the huge smooth white ball sitting on the ground, sometimes head-sized — \"remember it.\" Word travels before the lesson cools."
    },
    {
      "day": 31,
      "line": "Journal updated: colonies of umbrella-like leaves, single lemon-sized fruit hidden underneath grows here too — better than tall smooth stalks turning reddish-purple, with dark purple berry clusters in late summer."
    },
    {
      "day": 32,
      "line": "📖 LEARNED: Managing Fear (Level 1). Fear is data, not orders. Acknowledge it, then decide anyway. Courage is fear that kept going."
    },
    {
      "day": 36,
      "line": "◈ WORD TRAVELS — riders from The Red Table bring talk of Haven. Out there they call you the Feared. The show's narration lingers on your hands."
    },
    {
      "day": 38,
      "line": "Travel 3 tiles to meadow.\n— Open ground —\nThe grass is bent in a long smooth run, like something heavy slid through it. You walk the other way around."
    },
    {
      "day": 45,
      "line": "You notice the village gives you room on the path now. Not fear, exactly. Room."
    },
    {
      "day": 47,
      "line": "🔍 Klaus has been turning over tall smooth stalks turning reddish-purple, with dark purple berry clusters in late summer for days — today it clicked. \"I know this one now. Look — see the leaves?\""
    },
    {
      "day": 48,
      "line": "◈ WORD TRAVELS — riders from The Red Table bring talk of Haven. Out there they call you the Feared. The show's narration lingers on your hands."
    },
    {
      "day": 48,
      "line": "★ IDENTIFIED: Pokeweed. Smooth stalks, purple-red stems, dark berry clusters. Uses unknown — harvest, taste, and learn."
    },
    {
      "day": 48,
      "line": "💡 Pokeweed. The tall smooth stalks turning reddish-purple, with dark purple berry clusters in late summer you've been looking at for days finally has a name, and now you'll never unsee it."
    },
    {
      "day": 60,
      "line": "◈ WORD TRAVELS — riders from Emberhold bring talk of Haven. Out there they call you the Feared. The show's narration lingers on your hands."
    },
